  "2026-11-14T10:55:53.603Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Failure -> cause -> fix: raw Mermaid export of 36 long-identity fixture nodes now exits 2 -> GH-1678 (pm-cli CHANGELOG 2026.11.8) enforces the custom renderer byte budget, correctly measuring 7736 tokens against the unchanged 4000-token default -> exercise the existing root/depth shaping for a valid small raw document, and retain the entire large fixture as an explicit output_budget_exceeded refusal (requested_budget_infeasible, exit 2, default budget 4000, measured tokens above budget). Full structured export with an explicit unbounded control must still return every fixture row. Keep the before-write file/control refusal and add an authoritative tracker fingerprint check. No production code, thresholds or row-count requirements changed."
  "2026-11-14T10:57:50.249Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Final linked focused run passes 3/3 tests with zero failures, cancellations or skips: bounded raw document plus oversized default-budget refusal and complete structured export, compact file receipts, and diagram/control behavior. The oversized refusal is checked in TOON, retaining its 4000-token ceiling; JSON has a distinct 6000-token default, so the test does not compare those format-specific defaults. Authoritative tracker bytes remain unchanged. npm/Bun typecheck, build:test, lint, zero-duplication gate (0%, unchanged 0% threshold), and docstrings (220 declarations) pass. Original current-pin raw case fails exit 2 before adaptation, providing migration revert proof. Full npm/Bun release checks remain queued serially at unchanged coverage thresholds."
